      "side": 1,
      "message": "The test is validating that the IPMI Get Self Test Results command is implemented correctly and returns a valid IPMI-defined response, not that a specific platform always passes self-test.\n\nWith the recent implementation, valid responses can now include:\n\n55h \u003d All tests passed\n57h \u003d Inaccessible/unavailable devices or services detected\n56h \u003d Not implemented (kept for compatibility with older builds)\n\nQEMU returns 57 a0 because FRU and/or SEL are not fully available in that environment, which is expected. Since the purpose is interface compliance rather than platform health verification, an environment-specific expectation should not be required for this test.",
